{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_396041a641794214f945b7487fc15568d7f2fbaba9f8d8cb2414e95ec75585e1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"LLM configuration is provided in a taskweaver_config.json file, e.g. llm.api_key and llm.model for OpenAI, with other LLMs and advanced configurations supported per the docs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5ac28aad81a5ae6cfe17a91db831a4ac7d2ed9a3e3c3399ae4f4e0ff794fdd89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"TaskWeaver is described as a code-first agent framework for planning and executing data analytics tasks, interpreting user requests as code snippets and coordinating plugin functions in a stateful manner."},{"claim_ids":["clm_60910a6d43a6c3bf0a3b78620a2f083192a2f3c9ab4ee2d91e81752d002e9516"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Unlike frameworks that track only chat history, TaskWeaver preserves both chat history and code execution history including in-memory data, which it says helps with complex data like high-dimensional tables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a571a048c660e12740a4e21bea33f2f7d58b575d9984f971272ff9a0f46a15e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project requires Python 3.10 or 3.11 per its README badge and states Python >= 3.10 is required for installation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e293afa843ba3217a57240a49c50f36ab825309a151c5e2327a4a597a426bb44"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"TaskWeaver can be used via a CLI (python -m taskweaver -p ./project/), a Web UI for demos, or imported as a library into existing projects."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fac63becd8b56d8a01633b936fbf73e6d433f4fa8295809020f0cda8b533c1e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: installation from source involves cloning the repo and running pip install -r requirements.txt; earlier versions can be installed from release tags via pip install git+https://github.com/microsoft/TaskWeaver@<TAG>."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fef015d078f924049fc7899d222735f8afbefb677c830d03c13eff7ab6f26ca1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sql_pull_data example plugin is implemented on top of Langchain and requires installing langchain and tabulate; the forecasting example requires yfinance and statsmodels."}],"claim_ids":["clm_396041a641794214f945b7487fc15568d7f2fbaba9f8d8cb2414e95ec75585e1","clm_5ac28aad81a5ae6cfe17a91db831a4ac7d2ed9a3e3c3399ae4f4e0ff794fdd89","clm_60910a6d43a6c3bf0a3b78620a2f083192a2f3c9ab4ee2d91e81752d002e9516","clm_a571a048c660e12740a4e21bea33f2f7d58b575d9984f971272ff9a0f46a15e4","clm_e293afa843ba3217a57240a49c50f36ab825309a151c5e2327a4a597a426bb44","clm_fac63becd8b56d8a01633b936fbf73e6d433f4fa8295809020f0cda8b533c1e8","clm_fef015d078f924049fc7899d222735f8afbefb677c830d03c13eff7ab6f26ca1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","id":"pg_253fb7512d345c6ebd8aee62964dd689","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-taskweaver-readme-md-d44ddef23f90-ee62964dd689.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0c30b6d7b0005bf9a831c3290ce0af2a"],"title":"microsoft/TaskWeaver/README.md @ d44ddef23f90","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_95887d86b45a2639936f150f85a3c2ec68c930febe311c533d8f4ef8eb820c9b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In the default flow, the user query goes to the Planner, which generates a plan for the CodeInterpreter; the interpreter executes and returns results, and the Planner summarizes them back, possibly iterating multiple times."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de4997394b6bac68582e9ff37a7e6f7572b8560d37671d47cd46a1277cf262b5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plugins consist of paired Python and YAML files in a plugins folder (e.g. ascii_render.py and ascii_render.yaml) with required fields such as parameters and returns; sample plugins include anomaly_detection, ascii_render, klarna_search, and tell_joke."}],"claim_ids":["clm_95887d86b45a2639936f150f85a3c2ec68c930febe311c533d8f4ef8eb820c9b","clm_de4997394b6bac68582e9ff37a7e6f7572b8560d37671d47cd46a1277cf262b5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e","id":"pg_71c75c2fbefa5530818e7752ffb8ad34","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-taskweaver-website-docs-faq-md-d44ddef23f90-7752ffb8ad34.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_252cbbd8f1ef5a58b191a93308faeb03"],"title":"microsoft/TaskWeaver/website/docs/FAQ.md @ d44ddef23f90","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:09:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fd6603a8e1d647659cf3cddf44d3483e"}
